      "writtenOn": "2022-08-10T09:10:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FYI, I think this significantly more overhead than just the SIOCGIFADDR approach, I imagine this is dumping all addresses on the system and then filtering by interface and then filtering by ipv4.\n\nSIOCGIFADDR will simply directly retrieve the single ipv4 address on the clat interface (and there\u0027s only 1 by definition).\n\nBut maybe performance here doesn\u0027t matter since this presumably triggers once during cell/wifi v6-only connect?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 865,
        "startChar": 69,
        "endLine": 865,
        "endChar": 85
