      "writtenOn": "2022-11-10T13:29:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "NetworkInterface dumps all (getAll) and filter out with a given interface name. \nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:libcore/ojluni/src/main/java/java/net/NetworkInterface.java;l\u003d314\n```\npublic static NetworkInterface getByName(String name) throws SocketException {\n        if (name \u003d\u003d null)\n            throw new NullPointerException();\n\n        // Android-changed: Rewrote NetworkInterface on top of Libcore.io.\n        NetworkInterface[] nis \u003d getAll();\n        for (NetworkInterface ni : nis) {\n            if (ni.getName().equals(name)) {\n                return ni;\n            }\n        }\n        return null;\n    }\n```\n\nupdateUpstreamNetworkState() is called by \n1. upstream capability change\nEVENT_ON_CAPABILITIES -\u003e handleNewUpstreamNetworkState\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/packages/modules/Connectivity/Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/Tethering.java;l\u003d2024\n2. upstream re-selection\nchooseUpstreamType -\u003e setUpstreamNetwork -\u003e handleNewUpstreamNetworkState\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Connectivity/Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/Tethering.java;l\u003d1832\n\nI think that if the upstream status is not changed frequently, maybe performance doesn\u0027t matter.\n\nHi Maze, Mark\nHow do you think? Thank you",
